# Run K (2026-11-07, user: "lets try privileged critic"): run I (pure SAC + PER,
# no noise pin, no cloning; slurm/il_finetune_c0_sac_per.env) with a PRIVILEGED
# CRITIC: PRIV_OBS=1 adds the route metres to the current goal (and a known flag)
# to the replay rows, read by the critic alone -- the actor and the GRU that feeds
# it never see them (actor_state_cols / core_state_cols, e53440c).
#
# Why: the offline diagnosis (scripts/offline_critic_slope.py) found the warm-up
# critic crediting the expert's braking approach for the +100 arrival, because it
# could not see how far the goal was: with the approach cut from its data the
# "steer left + less throttle" tilt vanished. The arrival speed rule STAYS (10
# km/h, v52_reward.env): without it lane following alone reached the goal (c0's
# wrong-goal success .65/.70), so braking at the goal is what makes the image
# matter -- and the critic now sees the distance that explains it.
#
# Live goal rows read info["route_remaining_m"] (ROUTE_POTENTIAL=1 in v52); HER
# rows the path metres to the hindsight goal; recorded episodes that reached their
# goal the driven-path metres to the stop; the rest (explore, failed recordings)
# 'unknown'. The full preload stays (arrivals included).
# Evals: VAL_OVERLAY=slurm/il_eval_val_chw_jr_priv.env, VAL_TAG=jr35 (the rows must
# carry the two columns to match the checkpoint; scoring identical to c0's jr35).
. "$REPO/slurm/il_finetune_c0_sac_per.env"
export PRIV_OBS=1
